WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Hello everyone, this is our training center and I'm giving a quick overview how the Turing machine works.

00:08.000 --> 00:13.000
First of all, you need to select the module Fundamentals of Computer Science.

00:13.000 --> 00:18.000
Then you have to select the topic of the Turing machines.

00:18.000 --> 00:27.000
Here we can go to the Simulation tab and just enter some Turing machine that we want.

00:27.000 --> 00:41.000
For example, one that can bit flip certain tape contents so that you can invert the tape.

00:41.000 --> 00:57.000
With our states set up, we can just enter something on the tape that is then getting inverted.

00:57.000 --> 01:10.000
You can just automatically let it play and watch the Turing machine invert tape contents until the entire tape is inverted.

01:10.000 --> 01:17.000
We can also go back to the configuration and change stuff around here.

01:17.000 --> 01:26.000
For example, add a new state or remove it or add new characters that also can do things on our machine.

01:26.000 --> 01:32.000
We can also export the whole machine to this compressed string format.

01:33.000 --> 01:44.000
We can copy that compressed string and when we just come back after doing something else, we can put the string in, can import it and our machine is back.

01:44.000 --> 01:53.000
We also have the possibility to watch some examples, like to look at some examples to get a better grasp of how everything works.

01:53.000 --> 02:02.000
For example, we can look at a binary increment, how you would basically increment this number by one.

02:02.000 --> 02:09.000
There are also exercises you can do, like inverting a binary word, basically what we just did.

02:09.000 --> 02:13.000
Then we can enter a machine, for example what we just did.

02:13.000 --> 02:17.000
We can check if the solution is right.

02:17.000 --> 02:27.000
So we halt in every way and every time, for example, we end it in a halt state and we pass the test.

02:27.000 --> 02:34.000
We can also load a pre-built solution, which is identical because I stole that example.

02:34.000 --> 02:41.000
And that's it about the Turing machine and with this short test video.
